(function(E){ const x = E["exam-06"] = E["exam-06"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x06-r2"] = {"id":"x06-r2","patterns":["RA-mind","GT2-business","PARA-research"],"title":{"en":"Reading 2: Passage 2 / Section 2","tr":"Reading 2: Passage 2 / Section 2","fa":"Reading ۲: متن ۲ (Passage 2) / بخش ۲ (Section 2)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to find which section contains a piece of information, complete a summary with one word from the passage, and choose two correct statements from five.","tr":"Bu derste bir bilginin hangi bölümde olduğunu bulmayı, bir özeti metinden tek kelimeyle tamamlamayı ve beş ifadeden doğru ikisini seçmeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری پیدا کنی یک اطلاعات در کدام بخش است، یک خلاصه را با یک کلمه از متن کامل کنی و از پنج جمله دو جمله‌ی درست را انتخاب کنی."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete a table and a flow-chart with one word from two work texts, reading across each row and following each stage in order.","tr":"Bu derste iki iş metninden tek kelimeyle bir tabloyu ve bir akış şemasını tamamlamayı, her satırı boydan boya okumayı ve her aşamayı sırayla izlemeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یک جدول و یک نمودار مراحل را با یک کلمه از دو متن کاری کامل کنی، هر ردیف را از اول تا آخر بخوانی و هر مرحله را به ترتیب دنبال کنی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 2: a report on a habit","tr":"Reading Passage 2: bir alışkanlık üzerine rapor","fa":"Reading Passage 2: گزارشی درباره‌ی یک عادت"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to find which section contains a piece of information, complete a summary with one word from the passage, and choose two correct statements from five.","tr":"Bu derste bir bilginin hangi bölümde olduğunu bulmayı, bir özeti metinden tek kelimeyle tamamlamayı ve beş ifadeden doğru ikisini seçmeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری پیدا کنی یک اطلاعات در کدام بخش است، یک خلاصه را با یک کلمه از متن کامل کنی و از پنج جمله دو جمله‌ی درست را انتخاب کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Sections","tr":"Bölüm","fa":"بخش"},"value":"A-F"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: why we put things off","tr":"Bu sınav: işleri neden erteleriz","fa":"این آزمون: چرا کارها را عقب می‌اندازیم"},"intro":{"en":"Psychology and the mind are among the most common Academic subjects. A report like this moves from what the problem is, to its causes and costs, to possible solutions, with researchers quoted along the way.","tr":"Psikoloji ve zihin en sık çıkan Academic konuları arasındadır. Böyle bir rapor sorunun ne olduğundan nedenlerine ve maliyetlerine, oradan olası çözümlere geçer; yol boyunca araştırmacılardan alıntı yapar.","fa":"روان‌شناسی و ذهن از رایج‌ترین موضوع‌های Academic هستند. گزارشی مثل این از چیستیِ مشکل به علت‌ها و هزینه‌ها و بعد به راه‌حل‌های ممکن می‌رسد و در طول مسیر از پژوهشگرها نقل‌قول می‌کند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x06-r2-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-mind","PARA-research"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-mind","n":30,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 30 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 30’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۰ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Why people delay, and what helps","tr":"İnsanlar neden erteler ve ne işe yarar","fa":"چرا آدم‌ها کار را عقب می‌اندازند و چه کمکی می‌کند"},"asks":{"en":"A report in six lettered sections on a habit of the mind: what it really is, why it feels good, who does it most, what it costs, what does not work and what does. Researchers are quoted along the way.","tr":"Zihnin bir alışkanlığı hakkında harflerle ayrılmış altı bölümlük bir rapor: gerçekte ne olduğu, neden iyi hissettirdiği, en çok kimin yaptığı, neye mal olduğu, neyin işe yaramadığı ve neyin yaradığı. Yol boyunca araştırmacılardan alıntılar var.","fa":"گزارشی در شش بخشِ حرف‌دار درباره‌ی یک عادت ذهنی: واقعاً چیست، چرا حس خوبی می‌دهد، چه کسانی بیشتر دچارش می‌شوند، چه هزینه‌ای دارد، چه چیزی کمک نمی‌کند و چه چیزی کمک می‌کند. در طول متن از پژوهشگرها نقل‌قول می‌شود."},"fields":["What it is","Why delay feels good","Who delays most","The costs","What does not work","What helps"],"words":[{"a":"put off","b":"delay / leave until later / procrastinate","tr":"ertelemek","fa":"عقب انداختن"},{"a":"relief","b":"feeling better at once","tr":"rahatlama","fa":"آسودگی"},{"a":"short-lived","b":"does not last long","tr":"kısa süreli","fa":"کوتاه‌مدت"},{"a":"linked to","b":"connected with / associated with","tr":"... ile bağlantılı","fa":"مرتبط با"},{"a":"afraid","b":"worried / fear that","tr":"korkan","fa":"ترسیده، نگران"},{"a":"on average","b":"in general / typically","tr":"ortalamada","fa":"به‌طور میانگین"},{"a":"penalties","b":"fines / extra charges","tr":"cezalar","fa":"جریمه‌ها"},{"a":"rarely succeed","b":"seldom work / are unlikely to help","tr":"nadiren işe yarar","fa":"به‌ندرت جواب می‌دهد"},{"a":"harsh","b":"very critical / unkind","tr":"sert","fa":"سخت‌گیر، تند"},{"a":"forgive yourself","b":"stop blaming yourself","tr":"kendini affetmek","fa":"خودت را بخشیدن"},{"a":"divide into","b":"break into smaller parts","tr":"... bölmek","fa":"تقسیم کردن به"}],"traps":[{"en":"Same word, wrong section: \"costs\" appear in more than one section, but only one describes money paid as a result of delay.","tr":"Aynı kelime, yanlış bölüm: \"maliyet\" birden fazla bölümde geçebilir ama yalnızca biri gecikme yüzünden ödenen parayı anlatır.","fa":"کلمه‌ی یکسان، بخش غلط: «هزینه» ممکن است در چند بخش بیاید، اما فقط یکی پولی را توصیف می‌کند که به‌خاطر تأخیر پرداخت می‌شود."},{"en":"Choose TWO: an option can repeat words from the passage but say the opposite: \"caused by laziness\" when the text says it is not laziness.","tr":"İKİ seç: bir seçenek metindeki kelimeleri tekrarlayıp tersini söyleyebilir: metin tembellik olmadığını söylerken \"tembellikten kaynaklanır\".","fa":"دو تا انتخاب کن: یک گزینه ممکن است کلمه‌های متن را تکرار کند ولی برعکس را بگوید: «ناشی از تنبلی» وقتی متن می‌گوید تنبلی نیست."},{"en":"Summary from the passage: the gap needs one word in the exact form: a past verb after \"who\", a plural after \"small\".","tr":"Metinden özet: boşluk tam biçimiyle tek bir kelime ister: \"who\"dan sonra geçmiş zaman fiil, \"small\"dan sonra çoğul.","fa":"خلاصه از روی متن: جای خالی یک کلمه به همان شکل دقیق می‌خواهد: بعد از «who» فعل گذشته، بعد از «small» جمع."}],"example":{"text":"Question: \"Which section contains a reference to a link that is not fully understood?\"","item":"(a) \"People who exercise in the morning sleep better, although researchers are not sure why.\" (b) \"People who exercise in the morning sleep better.\"","answer":"(a)","why":{"en":"\"Tend to sleep better\" is the link; \"not sure why\" = not fully understood.","tr":"\"Daha iyi uyuma eğiliminde\" bağlantıdır; \"neden olduğundan emin değiller\" = tam anlaşılmamış.","fa":"«معمولاً بهتر می‌خوابند» ارتباط است؛ «مطمئن نیستند چرا» یعنی کاملاً فهمیده نشده."}}},{"id":"RA-mind-report","ctx":["RA-mind"],"title":{"en":"Reports on learning, the mind and society","tr":"Öğrenme, zihin ve toplum üzerine raporlar","fa":"گزارش درباره‌ی یادگیری، ذهن و جامعه"},"asks":{"en":"A report on how people learn, think or behave: bilingual children, boredom, play, mixed-ability classes, putting things off. Paragraphs describe research, explanations and practical advice.","tr":"İnsanların nasıl öğrendiği, düşündüğü ya da davrandığı üzerine bir rapor: iki dilli çocuklar, can sıkıntısı, oyun, karma düzeyli sınıflar, işleri erteleme. Paragraflar araştırmaları, açıklamaları ve pratik tavsiyeleri anlatır.","fa":"گزارشی درباره‌ی اینکه آدم‌ها چطور یاد می‌گیرند، فکر می‌کنند یا رفتار می‌کنند: بچه‌های دوزبانه، کسالت، بازی، کلاس‌های چندسطحی، عقب انداختن کارها. پاراگراف‌ها پژوهش‌ها، توضیح‌ها و توصیه‌های کاربردی را شرح می‌دهند."},"fields":["A popular belief challenged","The benefits for older learners","A practical suggestion for teachers","How the research was carried out","Which paragraph mentions the age of the participants?"],"words":[{"a":"a common belief","b":"many people assume / it is widely thought","tr":"yaygın bir inanış","fa":"باوری رایج"},{"a":"challenge","b":"question / cast doubt on","tr":"sorgulamak","fa":"زیر سؤال بردن"},{"a":"evidence","b":"studies show / data suggest","tr":"kanıt","fa":"شواهد"},{"a":"advantage","b":"benefit / gain","tr":"avantaj","fa":"مزیت"},{"a":"practical advice","b":"tips / what teachers can do","tr":"pratik tavsiye","fa":"توصیه‌ی کاربردی"},{"a":"lasting effect","b":"years later / long-term","tr":"kalıcı etki","fa":"اثر ماندگار"},{"a":"participants","b":"volunteers / subjects","tr":"katılımcılar","fa":"شرکت‌کننده‌ها"},{"a":"age group","b":"children aged six to nine","tr":"yaş grubu","fa":"گروه سنی"},{"a":"behaviour","b":"what people do / how they act","tr":"davranış","fa":"رفتار"},{"a":"motivation","b":"the reason people try","tr":"motivasyon","fa":"انگیزه"},{"a":"concentration","b":"focus / attention","tr":"dikkat","fa":"تمرکز"},{"a":"the role of","b":"how ... contributes to","tr":"... -in rolü","fa":"نقشِ"}],"traps":[{"en":"A heading that repeats a word from the paragraph is often wrong. Match the idea, not the word.","tr":"Paragraftaki bir kelimeyi tekrarlayan başlık çoğu zaman yanlıştır. Kelimeyi değil, fikri eşleştir.","fa":"عنوانی که یک کلمه‌ی پاراگراف را تکرار می‌کند اغلب غلط است. ایده را جور کن، نه کلمه را."},{"en":"Matching information can use the same letter twice: one paragraph may answer two questions.","tr":"Bilgi eşleştirmede aynı harf iki kez kullanılabilir: bir paragraf iki soruyu cevaplayabilir.","fa":"در جورکردن اطلاعات یک حرف ممکن است دو بار بیاید: یک پاراگراف می‌تواند جواب دو سؤال باشد."}],"example":{"text":"B  It is often said that boredom is simply a waste of time. Recent work suggests the opposite: people who did a dull task before a creative one produced more original ideas than those who went straight to the creative task.","item":"Choose the heading for paragraph B:  i  A popular view of boredom questioned   ii  Ways to avoid boredom at work   iii  Why creative tasks are dull","answer":"i","why":{"en":"\"It is often said... Recent work suggests the opposite\" = a common belief challenged.","tr":"\"Sık söylenir... Yeni çalışmalar tersini gösteriyor\" = sorgulanan yaygın bir inanış.","fa":"«اغلب گفته می‌شود... پژوهش‌های تازه خلافش را نشان می‌دهند» = باوری رایج که زیر سؤال رفته."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-mind"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-mind","n":30,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 30 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 30’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۰ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Three tasks on one passage","tr":"Bir metin üzerinde üç görev","fa":"سه تمرین روی یک متن"},"body":{"en":"Questions 14-16: which section, A-F, contains each piece of information? Questions 17-22: complete a summary with ONE WORD ONLY from the passage. Questions 23-24 and 25-26: choose TWO letters, A-E; each correct letter is one mark.","tr":"Soru 14-16: her bilgi A-F’den hangi bölümde? Soru 17-22: bir özeti metinden ONE WORD ONLY ile tamamla. Soru 23-24 ve 25-26: A-E’den İKİ harf seç; her doğru harf bir puan.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱۴ تا ۱۶: هر اطلاعات در کدام بخش، A تا F، است؟ سؤال‌های ۱۷ تا ۲۲: یک خلاصه را با ONE WORD ONLY از متن کامل کن. سؤال‌های ۲۳-۲۴ و ۲۵-۲۶: از A تا E دو حرف انتخاب کن؛ هر حرف درست یک نمره است."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Find the part of the passage first","tr":"Önce metnin ilgili kısmını bul","fa":"اول بخش مربوط متن را پیدا کن"},"steps":[{"en":"Read the summary title: it tells you which sections the summary covers.","tr":"Özet başlığını oku: özetin hangi bölümleri kapsadığını söyler.","fa":"عنوان خلاصه را بخوان: می‌گوید خلاصه کدام بخش‌ها را پوشش می‌دهد."},{"en":"For each gap, decide the word class from the grammar, then find the paraphrase in the passage.","tr":"Her boşluk için dil bilgisinden kelime türüne karar ver, sonra metinde başka sözcüklerle söylenişini bul.","fa":"برای هر جای خالی از روی دستور نوع کلمه را مشخص کن و بعد بیان دیگرش را در متن پیدا کن."},{"en":"For choose TWO, check each of the five options against the text and mark it true, false or not mentioned.","tr":"İKİ seç sorularında beş seçeneğin her birini metinle karşılaştır ve doğru, yanlış ya da söz edilmemiş diye işaretle.","fa":"در «دو تا انتخاب کن»، هر پنج گزینه را با متن مقایسه کن و درست، غلط یا ذکرنشده علامت بزن."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"The opposite in the same words","tr":"Aynı kelimelerle tersi","fa":"برعکس، با همان کلمه‌ها"},"body":{"en":"Wrong options often use words from the passage in a way the passage rejects: \"people often assume X... It is not that... but...\" Read the whole sentence before you decide that an option is true.","tr":"Yanlış seçenekler çoğu zaman metindeki kelimeleri metnin reddettiği bir şekilde kullanır: \"insanlar çoğu zaman X sanır... Mesele ... değil, ... \" Bir seçeneğin doğru olduğuna karar vermeden önce cümlenin tamamını oku.","fa":"گزینه‌های غلط اغلب کلمه‌های متن را طوری به کار می‌برند که متن ردش می‌کند: «مردم اغلب فکر می‌کنند X... موضوع این نیست که...، بلکه...». قبل از اینکه درباره‌ی درست بودن یک گزینه تصمیم بگیری کل جمله را بخوان."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"A summary gap, step by step","tr":"Bir özet boşluğu, adım adım","fa":"یک جای خالی خلاصه، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Complete the summary. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.","text":"\"Workers who took short breaks every hour reported far less tiredness at the end of the day.\"","item":"Summary: Taking regular breaks reduced ___ at the end of the working day.","answer":"tiredness","walk":[{"en":"The gap follows \"reduced\", so it needs a noun.","tr":"Boşluk \"reduced\"dan sonra geliyor, yani bir isim gerekiyor.","fa":"جای خالی بعد از «reduced» است، پس اسم می‌خواهد."},{"en":"\"Far less tiredness\" = reduced tiredness; \"every hour\" = regular.","tr":"\"Çok daha az yorgunluk\" = azalmış yorgunluk; \"her saat\" = düzenli.","fa":"«خستگیِ خیلی کمتر» یعنی خستگیِ کم‌شده؛ «هر ساعت» یعنی منظم."},{"en":"Copy tiredness exactly. \"less tiredness\" would be two words.","tr":"tiredness’ı aynen kopyala. \"less tiredness\" iki kelime olur.","fa":"tiredness را دقیقاً کپی کن. «less tiredness» دو کلمه می‌شود."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"It is not that shy people dislike others, but that they fear being judged.\" Which option is TRUE?","options":["Shy people fear being judged.","Shy people dislike other people.","Shy people are rarely judged."],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"It is not that... but that...\" rejects the first idea and gives the real one.","tr":"\"Mesele ... değil, ... \" ilk fikri reddedip gerçek olanı veriyor.","fa":"«موضوع این نیست که...، بلکه...» ایده‌ی اول را رد می‌کند و ایده‌ی واقعی را می‌دهد."}},"remember":{"en":"Use the summary title to find the right sections, copy one word in its exact form, and check every choose-TWO option against the text.","tr":"Doğru bölümleri bulmak için özet başlığını kullan, tek kelimeyi tam biçimiyle kopyala ve her İKİ seç seçeneğini metinle karşılaştır.","fa":"از عنوان خلاصه برای پیدا کردن بخش‌های درست استفاده کن، یک کلمه را به شکل دقیقش کپی کن و هر گزینه‌ی «دو تا انتخاب کن» را با متن بسنج."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x06-r2-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r2"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 2","title":{"en":"Tomorrow, definitely","tr":"Yarın, kesinlikle","fa":"فردا، حتماً"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-mind"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.","passage":"Tomorrow, definitely\n\nA  Almost everyone puts things off. We delay replying to an awkward email, leave a report until the night before it is due, or tidy the kitchen instead of filling in a tax form. For a long time, this habit was treated as a simple failure of discipline, a sign that the person concerned was lazy or disorganised. Over the past thirty years, however, psychologists have built up a rather different picture. Procrastination, they argue, has less to do with managing time than with managing feelings. Most people who put things off know perfectly well how long a task will take; what they struggle with is the discomfort of starting it. Surveys suggest that the problem is widespread among students and office workers alike, and that it is not limited to unpleasant jobs: people also delay tasks they actually want to do, such as writing to an old friend.\n\nB  The key idea is what researchers call mood repair. When a task makes us anxious, bored or uncertain, avoiding it brings immediate relief. \"The moment you close the document, you feel better,\" explains the psychologist Marta Lindqvist. \"Your brain learns that delay is rewarded, and so the habit grows stronger each time.\" The problem is that the relief is short-lived, while the task does not go away. In effect, people trade a small improvement in how they feel now for a larger problem later, a pattern that Lindqvist describes as giving our future selves a job we do not want to do. Interestingly, brain-imaging studies suggest that many people think about their future selves in much the same way as they think about strangers, which may make it easier to leave problems for them.\n\nC  Not everyone procrastinates to the same degree. Studies consistently link frequent delay with impulsiveness and with low confidence in one's own abilities. Perfectionists are also at risk, though not for the reason people often assume. It is not that they care too much about detail, but that they are afraid the finished work will not be good enough, so they avoid starting at all. There is also an encouraging finding about age: on average, people procrastinate less as they get older, perhaps because they have learned from the consequences. Some researchers also point to the modern environment, in which a phone offers an instant escape from any task that feels difficult.\n\nD  Those consequences can be serious. Students who habitually delay tend to get lower grades and report higher levels of stress, especially as deadlines approach. Outside education, the costs are often financial: people who put off paperwork pay penalties for late tax returns, miss the deadlines for cheaper insurance, and save less for retirement. There is also growing evidence of an effect on health. Frequent procrastinators sleep worse, and they are more likely to delay seeing a doctor when something is wrong, which can turn a minor problem into a serious one.\n\nE  Given all this, it might seem that the answer is simply to try harder. Yet strategies based on willpower alone rarely succeed, because they do not deal with the feelings that caused the delay in the first place. Being harsh on yourself is particularly unhelpful. \"Criticising yourself adds one more unpleasant feeling to the task,\" says Lindqvist, \"and that makes avoiding it even more attractive.\" Productivity apps are popular, but researchers are doubtful about them too. On their own, they help people to plan, but planning was rarely the problem. A beautifully organised list of tasks can even become another way of avoiding the work itself, as people spend an hour arranging what they ought to be doing.\n\nF  So what does work? One surprising answer is kindness. In a study by the education researcher Daniel Okoro, students who forgave themselves for delaying their revision before a first exam procrastinated noticeably less before the next one. Okoro believes that forgiveness removes the guilt that people would otherwise try to escape by avoiding the task again. Practical techniques also help. It is easier to begin when a large task is divided into small steps, each of which can be completed in one sitting. Many people benefit from making a specific plan that states exactly when and where they will do something, rather than a vague intention to do it \"soon\". Finally, Lindqvist recommends starting with a first step so tiny that it feels almost silly, such as simply opening the file. \"Once you have started,\" she says, \"the task is rarely as bad as you imagined.\" None of these methods works for everyone, but together they suggest that the most effective approach is to make starting easier, rather than to make failing feel worse.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 14-16. Reading Passage 2 has six sections, A-F. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 14-16 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-info","bank":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"questions":[{"n":14,"kind":"match","prompt":"a reference to money that people lose because they delay","correct":3,"evidence":"people who put off paperwork pay penalties for late tax returns","why":{"en":"D: people \"pay penalties for late tax returns\" and miss cheaper insurance. Section B talks about cost only in the sense of a \"larger problem later\".","tr":"D: insanlar \"geç vergi beyannamesi için ceza ödüyor\" ve daha ucuz sigortayı kaçırıyor. B bölümü maliyetten yalnızca \"sonra daha büyük bir sorun\" anlamında söz ediyor.","fa":"D: آدم‌ها «برای اظهارنامه‌ی مالیاتی دیرهنگام جریمه می‌دهند» و بیمه‌ی ارزان‌تر را از دست می‌دهند. بخش B فقط به معنای «مشکلی بزرگ‌تر در آینده» از هزینه حرف می‌زند."},"trap":["TR-samewords","TR-detail"]},{"n":15,"kind":"match","prompt":"an explanation of why delaying a task can feel rewarding","correct":1,"evidence":"avoiding it brings immediate relief","why":{"en":"B: \"avoiding it brings immediate relief... delay is rewarded\".","tr":"B: \"ondan kaçınmak anında rahatlama getiriyor... erteleme ödüllendiriliyor\".","fa":"B: «پرهیز از آن آسودگی فوری می‌آورد... تأخیر پاداش می‌گیرد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":16,"kind":"match","prompt":"a mention of a group of people who tend to delay less","correct":2,"evidence":"people procrastinate less as they get older","why":{"en":"C: \"on average, people procrastinate less as they get older\" = older people.","tr":"C: \"ortalamada insanlar yaşlandıkça daha az erteliyor\" = yaşlılar.","fa":"C: «به‌طور میانگین آدم‌ها با بالا رفتن سن کمتر کار را عقب می‌اندازند» یعنی افراد مسن‌تر."},"trap":["TR-detail"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 17-22. Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 17-22 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"summary","summaryTitle":"What helps people stop putting things off","questions":[{"n":17,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Strategies that depend on ___ alone rarely work,","accept":["willpower"],"limit":1,"evidence":"strategies based on willpower alone rarely succeed","why":{"en":"\"Strategies based on willpower alone rarely succeed\": depend on = based on.","tr":"\"Yalnızca iradeye dayanan stratejiler nadiren başarılı olur\": depend on = based on.","fa":"«راهبردهایی که فقط بر اراده تکیه دارند به‌ندرت موفق می‌شوند»: depend on یعنی based on."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":18,"kind":"gap","prompt":"and being ___ on yourself makes the task even less attractive.","accept":["harsh"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Being harsh on yourself is particularly unhelpful","why":{"en":"\"Being harsh on yourself is particularly unhelpful\": it adds an unpleasant feeling.","tr":"\"Kendine sert davranmak özellikle zararlı\": hoş olmayan bir duygu ekliyor.","fa":"«با خودت سخت‌گیر بودن به‌خصوص بی‌فایده است»: یک حس ناخوشایند دیگر اضافه می‌کند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":19,"kind":"gap","prompt":"In one study, students who ___ themselves for an earlier delay put things off less before their next exam.","accept":["forgave"],"limit":1,"evidence":"students who forgave themselves for delaying their revision","why":{"en":"\"Students who forgave themselves for delaying their revision\": the past form fits \"who ___ themselves\".","tr":"\"Tekrarlarını ertelediği için kendini affeden öğrenciler\": geçmiş biçim \"who ___ themselves\" yapısına uyuyor.","fa":"«دانشجوهایی که خودشان را به‌خاطر عقب انداختن مرور بخشیدند»: شکل گذشته با «who ___ themselves» جور است."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":20,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The researcher believes forgiveness works because it removes ___.","accept":["guilt"],"limit":1,"evidence":"forgiveness removes the guilt","why":{"en":"\"Forgiveness removes the guilt that people would otherwise try to escape.\"","tr":"\"Affetmek, insanların başka türlü kaçmaya çalışacağı suçluluğu ortadan kaldırıyor.\"","fa":"«بخشیدن احساس گناهی را برمی‌دارد که آدم‌ها در غیر این صورت سعی می‌کنند از آن فرار کنند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":21,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Large tasks should be divided into small ___,","accept":["steps"],"limit":1,"evidence":"divided into small steps","why":{"en":"\"When a large task is divided into small steps.\" Plural.","tr":"\"Büyük bir görev küçük adımlara bölündüğünde.\" Çoğul.","fa":"«وقتی یک کار بزرگ به قدم‌های کوچک تقسیم شود». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":22,"kind":"gap","prompt":"and it helps to make a specific ___ saying when and where you will act.","accept":["plan"],"limit":1,"evidence":"making a specific plan that states exactly when and where","why":{"en":"\"A specific plan that states exactly when and where.\" One word, singular.","tr":"\"Tam olarak ne zaman ve nerede olacağını belirten belirli bir plan.\" Tek kelime, tekil.","fa":"«برنامه‌ای مشخص که دقیقاً می‌گوید کی و کجا». یک کلمه، مفرد."},"trap":["TR-limit"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 23-24. Choose TWO letters, A-E.","qtype":"mcq2","questions":[{"n":23,"n2":24,"kind":"mcq2","prompt":"Which TWO statements about people who often put things off are made in the passage?","options":["A They are usually lazy.","B They may fear that what they produce will fall short.","C They tend to sleep worse than other people.","D They are mostly students.","E They cannot judge how long a task will take."],"correct":[1,2],"evidence":"they are afraid the finished work will not be good enough","trap":["TR-samewords"],"why":{"en":"B: perfectionists fear the work \"will not be good enough\". C: \"frequent procrastinators sleep worse\". A is rejected in section A, E is contradicted (\"know perfectly well how long\"), and D is not stated.","tr":"B: mükemmeliyetçiler işin \"yeterince iyi olmayacağından\" korkuyor. C: \"sık erteleyenler daha kötü uyuyor\". A, A bölümünde reddediliyor, E ile çelişiliyor (\"ne kadar süreceğini gayet iyi biliyorlar\"), D ise söylenmiyor.","fa":"B: کمال‌گراها می‌ترسند کار «به اندازه‌ی کافی خوب نباشد». C: «کسانی که زیاد عقب می‌اندازند بدتر می‌خوابند». A در بخش A رد می‌شود، E نقض می‌شود («خیلی خوب می‌دانند چقدر طول می‌کشد») و D گفته نشده."}}]},{"instruction":"Questions 25-26. Choose TWO letters, A-E.","qtype":"mcq2","questions":[{"n":25,"n2":26,"kind":"mcq2","prompt":"Which TWO approaches does the writer say are unlikely to help?","options":["A forgiving yourself for past delays","B criticising yourself","C using a productivity app on its own","D dividing a task into small parts","E starting with a very small first step"],"correct":[1,2],"evidence":"Productivity apps are popular, but researchers are doubtful about them too","trap":["TR-paraphrase"],"why":{"en":"B: self-criticism \"adds one more unpleasant feeling\". C: apps \"on their own\" help only with planning. A, D and E are all recommended in section F.","tr":"B: kendini eleştirmek \"bir hoş olmayan duygu daha ekliyor\". C: uygulamalar \"tek başına\" yalnızca planlamaya yardım ediyor. A, D ve E’nin hepsi F bölümünde öneriliyor.","fa":"B: انتقاد از خود «یک حس ناخوشایند دیگر اضافه می‌کند». C: اپ‌ها «به‌تنهایی» فقط به برنامه‌ریزی کمک می‌کنند. A، D و E همه در بخش F توصیه شده‌اند."}}]}],"id":"c-x06-r2-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r2"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"The relief is short-lived.\" Short-lived means...","options":["very strong","coming too late","lasting only a short time"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Short-lived = it does not last long.","tr":"Short-lived = uzun sürmez.","fa":"short-lived یعنی زیاد دوام نمی‌آورد."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":2,"prompt":"A summary says \"depend on willpower\". Which words in a passage mean the same?","options":["free of willpower","based on willpower","instead of willpower"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"A strategy based on something depends on it.","tr":"Bir şeye dayanan strateji ona bağlıdır.","fa":"راهبردی که بر چیزی بنا شده به آن وابسته است."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Choose TWO from A-E. An option uses three words from the passage. What should you check?","options":["whether the passage says the same thing or the opposite","whether the words are spelled correctly","whether the option is the longest"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Matching words can hide an opposite meaning; check what the sentence actually says.","tr":"Eşleşen kelimeler zıt bir anlamı gizleyebilir; cümlenin gerçekte ne dediğine bak.","fa":"کلمه‌های یکسان ممکن است معنای برعکس را پنهان کنند؛ ببین جمله واقعاً چه می‌گوید."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"It is not that they dislike the work, but that they fear failing at it.\" Which option is a trap?","options":["They fear failing.","They are afraid of doing the work badly.","They dislike the work."],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"It is not that they dislike the work\" rejects this option.","tr":"\"İşi sevmedikleri için değil\" bu seçeneği reddediyor.","fa":"«موضوع این نیست که از کار بدشان می‌آید» این گزینه را رد می‌کند."}}],"id":"c-x06-r2-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r2"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 2: training and business stages","tr":"GT Reading Section 2: eğitim ve işletme aşamaları","fa":"GT Reading Section 2: آموزش و مرحله‌های کسب‌وکار"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete a table and a flow-chart with one word from two work texts, reading across each row and following each stage in order.","tr":"Bu derste iki iş metninden tek kelimeyle bir tabloyu ve bir akış şemasını tamamlamayı, her satırı boydan boya okumayı ve her aşamayı sırayla izlemeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یک جدول و یک نمودار مراحل را با یک کلمه از دو متن کاری کامل کنی، هر ردیف را از اول تا آخر بخوانی و هر مرحله را به ترتیب دنبال کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Texts","tr":"Metin","fa":"متن"},"value":"2"},{"label":{"en":"Word limit","tr":"Kelime sınırı","fa":"سقف کلمه"},"value":{"en":"1 word","tr":"1 kelime","fa":"۱ کلمه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: staff training and the life of a business","tr":"Bu sınav: personel eğitimi ve bir işletmenin yaşamı","fa":"این آزمون: آموزش کارکنان و زندگی یک کسب‌وکار"},"intro":{"en":"GT Section 2 is always about work. Texts on running a team or a business are common, and they are often organised with headings that match the rows of a table or the boxes of a flow-chart.","tr":"GT Section 2 her zaman işle ilgilidir. Bir ekibi ya da işletmeyi yönetmeyle ilgili metinler sık çıkar ve çoğu zaman bir tablonun satırlarına ya da bir akış şemasının kutularına uyan başlıklarla düzenlenir.","fa":"GT Section 2 همیشه درباره‌ی کار است. متن‌هایی درباره‌ی اداره‌ی تیم یا کسب‌وکار رایج‌اند و اغلب با عنوان‌هایی مرتب شده‌اند که با ردیف‌های جدول یا خانه‌های نمودار مراحل جورند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x06-r2gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT2-business"],"often":{"pattern":"GT2-business","n":16,"of":55,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 16 of the last 55 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 55 metnin 16’sında","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۶ متن از ۵۵ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Staff training and a growing business","tr":"Personel eğitimi ve büyüyen bir işletme","fa":"آموزش کارکنان و یک کسب‌وکارِ در حال رشد"},"asks":{"en":"Two texts for people who manage others: a guide to six kinds of staff training, which you use to complete a table, and a description of the four stages of a business, which you use to complete a flow-chart.","tr":"Başkalarını yöneten kişiler için iki metin: bir tabloyu doldurmak için kullandığın altı tür personel eğitimi rehberi ve bir akış şemasını doldurmak için kullandığın bir işletmenin dört aşamasının anlatımı.","fa":"دو متن برای کسانی که دیگران را مدیریت می‌کنند: راهنمایی درباره‌ی شش نوع آموزش کارکنان که با آن یک جدول را کامل می‌کنی، و توصیف چهار مرحله‌ی یک کسب‌وکار که با آن یک نمودار مراحل را کامل می‌کنی."},"fields":["Type of training","What it involves","Main benefit","Stage of the business","Main challenge"],"words":[{"a":"induction","b":"training for new staff in their first week","tr":"oryantasyon","fa":"آموزش بدو ورود"},{"a":"alongside","b":"next to / working with","tr":"yanında","fa":"در کنار"},{"a":"mentor","b":"an experienced person who gives advice","tr":"akıl hocası, mentor","fa":"منتور، راهنما"},{"a":"qualification","b":"a certificate or diploma","tr":"yeterlilik belgesi","fa":"مدرک"},{"a":"at your own pace","b":"as fast or slowly as you like","tr":"kendi hızında","fa":"با سرعت خودت"},{"a":"savings","b":"money you have put aside","tr":"birikim","fa":"پس‌انداز"},{"a":"run out of","b":"have none left","tr":"... tükenmek","fa":"تمام شدنِ"},{"a":"premises","b":"a building used by a business","tr":"işyeri binası","fa":"محل کسب‌وکار"},{"a":"investment","b":"money from outside the business","tr":"yatırım","fa":"سرمایه‌گذاری"},{"a":"innovate","b":"try new ideas and ways of working","tr":"yenilik yapmak","fa":"نوآوری کردن"},{"a":"decline","b":"a slow fall / getting worse","tr":"gerileme","fa":"افول"}],"traps":[{"en":"A table row has several facts. Read across the row: the gap in \"Main benefit\" is not the same as what the training involves.","tr":"Bir tablo satırında birkaç bilgi vardır. Satırı boydan boya oku: \"Main benefit\" sütunundaki boşluk, eğitimin içeriğiyle aynı şey değildir.","fa":"هر ردیف جدول چند اطلاعات دارد. ردیف را از اول تا آخر بخوان: جای خالیِ «Main benefit» با محتوای آموزش یکی نیست."},{"en":"ONE WORD ONLY: the text may say \"monthly rent\" or \"business rates\". Check which word is already printed in the box.","tr":"ONE WORD ONLY: metin \"monthly rent\" ya da \"business rates\" diyebilir. Kutuda hangi kelimenin zaten yazılı olduğuna bak.","fa":"ONE WORD ONLY: ممکن است متن «monthly rent» یا «business rates» بگوید. ببین کدام کلمه از قبل در خانه چاپ شده."}],"example":{"text":"\"Shadowing: a new employee follows a manager for a day. The main benefit is that they see how decisions are made.\"","item":"Table: Shadowing · main benefit: shows how ___ are made","answer":"decisions","why":{"en":"\"see how decisions are made\" = shows how decisions are made. Copy the plural.","tr":"\"Kararların nasıl verildiğini görmek\" = kararların nasıl verildiğini gösterir. Çoğulu kopyala.","fa":"«می‌بینند تصمیم‌ها چطور گرفته می‌شوند» یعنی نشان می‌دهد تصمیم‌ها چطور گرفته می‌شوند. جمع را کپی کن."}}},{"id":"GT2-business","ctx":["GT2-business"],"title":{"en":"Running a team or a small business","tr":"Bir ekibi ya da küçük bir işletmeyi yönetmek","fa":"اداره‌ی یک تیم یا یک کسب‌وکار کوچک"},"asks":{"en":"Workplace guides on meetings, projects, delegation, marketing, flexible working or types of training. Sentence and note completion test the advice and the steps.","tr":"Toplantılar, projeler, görev devri, pazarlama, esnek çalışma ya da eğitim türleri üzerine iş yeri rehberleri. Cümle ve not tamamlama tavsiyeleri ve adımları sınar.","fa":"راهنماهای محیط کار درباره‌ی جلسه، پروژه، واگذاری کار، بازاریابی، کار منعطف یا انواع آموزش. کامل کردن جمله و یادداشت توصیه‌ها و مرحله‌ها را می‌سنجد."},"fields":["Before a meeting, send the ___ to everyone.","Give tasks to staff who can do them ___.","Flexible hours must be agreed with your ___.","Training: on the job · external course · online"],"words":[{"a":"agenda","b":"list of points for the meeting","tr":"gündem","fa":"دستور جلسه"},{"a":"delegate","b":"give a task to someone else","tr":"görev devretmek","fa":"واگذار کردن"},{"a":"deadline","b":"the date it must be done by","tr":"son tarih","fa":"مهلت"},{"a":"budget","b":"the money available","tr":"bütçe","fa":"بودجه"},{"a":"priorities","b":"what matters most","tr":"öncelikler","fa":"اولویت‌ها"},{"a":"minutes","b":"written record of a meeting","tr":"toplantı tutanağı","fa":"صورت‌جلسه"},{"a":"colleague","b":"co-worker","tr":"iş arkadaşı","fa":"همکار"},{"a":"line manager","b":"the person you report to","tr":"bağlı olduğun yönetici","fa":"مدیر مستقیم"},{"a":"flexible hours","b":"choose when you start and finish","tr":"esnek çalışma saatleri","fa":"ساعت کاری منعطف"},{"a":"client","b":"customer","tr":"müşteri","fa":"مشتری"},{"a":"promote","b":"advertise / market","tr":"tanıtmak","fa":"تبلیغ کردن"},{"a":"progress","b":"how far the work has got","tr":"ilerleme","fa":"پیشرفت"}],"traps":[{"en":"The sentence to complete is a paraphrase; the gap word is copied from the text.","tr":"Tamamlanacak cümle başka sözcüklerle yazılmıştır; boşluktaki kelime metinden kopyalanır.","fa":"جمله‌ای که کامل می‌کنی با کلمه‌های دیگر نوشته شده؛ کلمه‌ی جای خالی از متن کپی می‌شود."},{"en":"Lists of advice: the question asks about one step (\"before the meeting\"); the text lists several.","tr":"Tavsiye listeleri: soru tek bir adımı sorar (\"toplantıdan önce\"); metin birkaçını sıralar.","fa":"فهرست توصیه‌ها: سؤال درباره‌ی یک مرحله است («قبل از جلسه»)؛ متن چند مرحله را می‌شمارد."}],"example":{"text":"Circulate the minutes within 24 hours, while decisions are still fresh. Each action point should name one person, not a whole department.","item":"Sentence: Each action point should name a single ___.   (ONE WORD ONLY)","answer":"person","why":{"en":"\"Name one person, not a whole department\": a single person.","tr":"\"Bütün bir bölümü değil, tek bir kişiyi yaz\": a single person.","fa":"«یک نفر را نام ببر، نه کل یک بخش را»: a single person."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT2-business"],"often":{"pattern":"GT2-business","n":16,"of":55,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 16 of the last 55 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 55 metnin 16’sında","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۶ متن از ۵۵ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"A table, then a flow-chart","tr":"Önce tablo, sonra akış şeması","fa":"اول جدول، بعد نمودار مراحل"},"body":{"en":"Questions 15-21: complete a table about the first text. Questions 22-27: complete a flow-chart about the second text. Both use ONE WORD ONLY from the text, and both follow the order of the text.","tr":"Soru 15-21: ilk metinle ilgili bir tabloyu tamamla. Soru 22-27: ikinci metinle ilgili bir akış şemasını tamamla. İkisi de metinden ONE WORD ONLY kullanır ve metnin sırasını izler.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱۵ تا ۲۱: جدولی درباره‌ی متن اول را کامل کن. سؤال‌های ۲۲ تا ۲۷: نمودار مراحلی درباره‌ی متن دوم را کامل کن. هر دو با ONE WORD ONLY از متن‌اند و ترتیب متن را دنبال می‌کنند."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Row headings and stage names","tr":"Satır başlıkları ve aşama adları","fa":"عنوان ردیف‌ها و اسم مرحله‌ها"},"steps":[{"en":"Match each row of the table to a heading in the text: Induction, Mentoring, E-learning.","tr":"Tablonun her satırını metindeki bir başlıkla eşleştir: Induction, Mentoring, E-learning.","fa":"هر ردیف جدول را با یک عنوان در متن جور کن: Induction، Mentoring، E-learning."},{"en":"Read the column heading too: \"what it involves\" and \"main benefit\" need different facts.","tr":"Sütun başlığını da oku: \"what it involves\" ve \"main benefit\" farklı bilgiler ister.","fa":"عنوان ستون را هم بخوان: «what it involves» و «main benefit» اطلاعات متفاوتی می‌خواهند."},{"en":"For the flow-chart, find the stage, then the one word that completes the box.","tr":"Akış şeması için önce aşamayı, sonra kutuyu tamamlayan tek kelimeyi bul.","fa":"برای نمودار مراحل اول مرحله را پیدا کن و بعد کلمه‌ای که خانه را کامل می‌کند."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"The word that is already there","tr":"Zaten orada olan kelime","fa":"کلمه‌ای که از قبل هست"},"body":{"en":"Boxes are short, so they often print part of the phrase: \"personal ___\", \"outside ___\". Write only the missing word, in the form the text uses. Writing the whole phrase breaks the limit.","tr":"Kutular kısadır, bu yüzden çoğu zaman ifadenin bir kısmı yazılıdır: \"personal ___\", \"outside ___\". Yalnızca eksik kelimeyi, metnin kullandığı biçimde yaz. İfadenin tamamını yazmak sınırı aşar.","fa":"خانه‌ها کوتاه‌اند، پس اغلب بخشی از عبارت چاپ شده: «personal ___»، «outside ___». فقط کلمه‌ی جاافتاده را به شکلی که متن آورده بنویس. نوشتن کل عبارت از سقف بیشتر می‌شود."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One table gap, step by step","tr":"Bir tablo boşluğu, adım adım","fa":"یک جای خالی جدول، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Complete the table. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","text":"\"Coaching: a manager meets an employee every week to set goals. The main advantage is that progress is checked regularly.\"","item":"Coaching | weekly meetings to set ___ | progress checked regularly","answer":"goals","walk":[{"en":"The row is Coaching; the gap is in the \"What it involves\" column.","tr":"Satır Coaching; boşluk \"What it involves\" sütununda.","fa":"ردیف Coaching است؛ جای خالی در ستون «What it involves»."},{"en":"\"meets an employee every week\" = weekly meetings.","tr":"\"Her hafta bir çalışanla görüşüyor\" = haftalık görüşmeler.","fa":"«هر هفته با یک کارمند جلسه دارد» یعنی جلسه‌های هفتگی."},{"en":"Write goals, plural, as in the text.","tr":"Metindeki gibi çoğul olarak goals yaz.","fa":"goals را مثل متن به شکل جمع بنویس."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Flow-chart box: \"Staff complete a short online ___ (ONE WORD ONLY)\". The text says \"staff then complete a short online assessment\". What do you write?","options":["online assessment","assessment","assessments"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"short online\" is printed; copy the singular form from the text: assessment.","tr":"\"short online\" yazılı; metindeki tekil biçimi kopyala: assessment.","fa":"«short online» چاپ شده؛ شکل مفرد را از متن کپی کن: assessment."}},"remember":{"en":"Find the row or stage first, read the column heading, and write only the missing word in the text’s form.","tr":"Önce satırı ya da aşamayı bul, sütun başlığını oku ve yalnızca eksik kelimeyi metindeki biçimiyle yaz.","fa":"اول ردیف یا مرحله را پیدا کن، عنوان ستون را بخوان و فقط کلمه‌ی جاافتاده را به شکل متن بنویس."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x06-r2-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r2"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 2","title":{"en":"Staff training and a growing business","tr":"Personel eğitimi ve büyüyen bir işletme","fa":"آموزش کارکنان و یک کسب‌وکار در حال رشد"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT2-business"],"texts":[{"title":"Staff training at Brightwell Foods: a guide for line managers","kind":"training guide","body":"Brightwell offers several kinds of training. This guide explains each one, so that you can choose what suits the members of your team.\n\nInduction\nEvery new employee takes part in a two-day induction during their first week. It covers health and safety and introduces company policies, from holidays to the use of social media. Staff who complete a proper induction settle in more quickly and are much less likely to leave in their first year.\n\nOn-the-job training\nMost practical skills are learned by doing the job alongside an experienced colleague, who shows the trainee each task and then watches them do it. Because no one has to leave the workplace, the main advantage of this method is its low cost.\n\nMentoring\nA mentor is a senior employee from a different department who meets a less experienced member of staff once a month to talk about their work and their future. Mentors do not teach particular skills. The real benefit is that the person being mentored gains confidence, especially when facing new responsibilities.\n\nJob rotation\nSome staff, particularly those who may become managers, spend a few weeks in each of several departments. They return with a much wider understanding of how the business works and how their own job affects others.\n\nExternal courses\nColleges and professional bodies run courses that lead to a recognised qualification. These are more expensive, and staff may be away from work for several days, so they need to be approved by a senior manager.\n\nE-learning\nOur online modules cover topics such as customer service and data protection. Staff can complete them at their own pace, at work or at home, which suits people who work part-time or on shifts.\n\nIf you are unsure which option is best, please contact the training team. Remember that most employees benefit from a mix of methods, and that training should be reviewed at each annual appraisal."},{"title":"From start-up to established business: the four stages","kind":"business guide","body":"Most successful small businesses pass through four stages. Knowing which stage you are in helps you to focus on the right problems at the right time. The stages are not always neat, and some businesses move backwards as well as forwards, but the pattern is surprisingly common across very different industries.\n\nStage 1: Start-up\nIn the early months, the owner usually does almost everything, from making the product to answering the phone. Few banks will lend to a business with no history, so most owners rely on their personal savings or borrow from family and friends. The greatest danger at this stage is simply running out of cash before the business has enough regular customers to survive.\n\nStage 2: Growth\nOnce sales begin to rise steadily, the owner can no longer do everything alone and starts to hire the first employees. This is often a difficult moment, because the owner has to learn to trust other people with the work. As orders increase, the business also needs clear systems for taking orders, sending invoices and paying suppliers. Without them, mistakes multiply, and customers who were happy with a small business may quickly lose patience.\n\nStage 3: Expansion\nAt this stage the business may open new premises, sell in other regions or launch new products. Expansion usually costs more than the business can pay for from its own profits, so many owners look for outside investment, either from a bank or from investors who take a share of the company in return.\n\nStage 4: Maturity\nEventually growth slows. The business is well known and has loyal customers, but there is a risk that it becomes too comfortable. Competitors copy its ideas, and tastes change. To avoid a slow decline, a mature business must continue to innovate, whether by improving its products, finding new customers or changing the way it works."}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 15-21. Complete the table below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"table","table":{"title":"Training at Brightwell Foods","headers":["Type","What it involves","Main benefit"],"rows":[["Induction","health and safety; introduces company (15) ___","new staff (16) ___ in more quickly"],["On-the-job training","learning alongside an experienced (17) ___","low cost"],["Mentoring","monthly meetings with a senior employee","the employee gains (18) ___"],["Job rotation","a few weeks in several departments","a wider (19) ___ of the business"],["External courses","lead to a recognised (20) ___","-"],["E-learning","online modules","staff work at their own (21) ___"]]},"questions":[{"n":15,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Induction · introduces company ___","accept":["policies"],"limit":1,"evidence":"introduces company policies","why":{"en":"\"It covers health and safety and introduces company policies.\" Plural.","tr":"\"Sağlık ve güvenliği kapsıyor ve şirket politikalarını tanıtıyor.\" Çoğul.","fa":"«ایمنی و بهداشت را پوشش می‌دهد و سیاست‌های شرکت را معرفی می‌کند». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":16,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Induction · benefit: new staff ___ in more quickly","accept":["settle"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Staff who complete a proper induction settle in more quickly","why":{"en":"\"Settle in more quickly\": \"in\" is printed after the gap.","tr":"\"Daha hızlı alışıyorlar\": \"in\" boşluktan sonra yazılı.","fa":"«زودتر جا می‌افتند»: «in» بعد از جای خالی چاپ شده."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":17,"kind":"gap","prompt":"On-the-job training · learning alongside an experienced ___","accept":["colleague"],"limit":1,"evidence":"alongside an experienced colleague","why":{"en":"\"Doing the job alongside an experienced colleague.\"","tr":"\"İşi deneyimli bir iş arkadaşının yanında yaparak.\"","fa":"«انجام کار در کنار یک همکار باتجربه»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":18,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Mentoring · benefit: the employee gains ___","accept":["confidence"],"limit":1,"evidence":"the person being mentored gains confidence","why":{"en":"Mentors do not teach skills; \"the person being mentored gains confidence\".","tr":"Mentorlar beceri öğretmez; \"mentorluk alan kişi özgüven kazanır\".","fa":"منتورها مهارت یاد نمی‌دهند؛ «کسی که راهنمایی می‌شود اعتمادبه‌نفس پیدا می‌کند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":19,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Job rotation · benefit: a wider ___ of the business","accept":["understanding"],"limit":1,"evidence":"a much wider understanding of how the business works","why":{"en":"\"A much wider understanding of how the business works.\" \"wider\" is printed.","tr":"\"İşletmenin nasıl işlediğine dair çok daha geniş bir anlayış.\" \"wider\" yazılı.","fa":"«درکی خیلی گسترده‌تر از اینکه کسب‌وکار چطور کار می‌کند». «wider» چاپ شده."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":20,"kind":"gap","prompt":"External courses · lead to a recognised ___","accept":["qualification"],"limit":1,"evidence":"courses that lead to a recognised qualification","why":{"en":"\"Courses that lead to a recognised qualification.\"","tr":"\"Tanınan bir yeterlilik belgesiyle sonuçlanan kurslar.\"","fa":"«دوره‌هایی که به یک مدرک معتبر می‌رسند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":21,"kind":"gap","prompt":"E-learning · staff work at their own ___","accept":["pace"],"limit":1,"evidence":"complete them at their own pace","why":{"en":"\"Staff can complete them at their own pace.\"","tr":"\"Personel onları kendi hızında tamamlayabilir.\"","fa":"«کارکنان می‌توانند آن‌ها را با سرعت خودشان تمام کنند»."},"trap":["TR-limit"]}]},{"text":1,"instruction":"Questions 22-27. Complete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"flow-chart","notesTitle":"The four stages of a business","questions":[{"n":22,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Start-up · most owners use their personal ___","accept":["savings"],"limit":1,"evidence":"most owners rely on their personal savings or borrow from family","why":{"en":"\"Rely on their personal savings\": \"personal\" is printed. Plural.","tr":"\"Kişisel birikimlerine güvenirler\": \"personal\" yazılı. Çoğul.","fa":"«به پس‌انداز شخصی‌شان تکیه می‌کنند»: «personal» چاپ شده. جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":23,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Start-up · greatest danger: running out of ___","accept":["cash"],"limit":1,"evidence":"simply running out of cash","why":{"en":"\"The greatest danger at this stage is simply running out of cash.\"","tr":"\"Bu aşamadaki en büyük tehlike basitçe nakdin tükenmesi.\"","fa":"«بزرگ‌ترین خطر در این مرحله این است که پول نقد تمام شود»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":24,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Growth · the owner hires the first ___","accept":["employees"],"limit":1,"evidence":"starts to hire the first employees","why":{"en":"\"Starts to hire the first employees.\" Plural.","tr":"\"İlk çalışanları işe almaya başlar.\" Çoğul.","fa":"«شروع می‌کند به استخدام اولین کارمندها». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":25,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Growth · introduce clear ___ for orders and payments","accept":["systems"],"limit":1,"evidence":"the business also needs clear systems for taking orders","why":{"en":"\"Clear systems for taking orders, sending invoices and paying suppliers.\"","tr":"\"Sipariş almak, fatura göndermek ve tedarikçilere ödeme yapmak için net sistemler.\"","fa":"«سیستم‌های روشن برای گرفتن سفارش، فرستادن فاکتور و پرداخت به تأمین‌کننده‌ها»."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":26,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Expansion · many owners look for outside ___","accept":["investment"],"limit":1,"evidence":"many owners look for outside investment","why":{"en":"\"Look for outside investment, either from a bank or from investors.\" \"outside\" is printed.","tr":"\"Bir bankadan ya da yatırımcılardan dış yatırım ararlar.\" \"outside\" yazılı.","fa":"«به دنبال سرمایه‌گذاریِ بیرونی می‌روند، از بانک یا از سرمایه‌گذارها». «outside» چاپ شده."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":27,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Maturity · the business must continue to ___","accept":["innovate"],"limit":1,"evidence":"a mature business must continue to innovate","why":{"en":"\"To avoid a slow decline, a mature business must continue to innovate.\" A verb after \"to\".","tr":"\"Yavaş bir gerilemeden kaçınmak için olgun bir işletme yenilik yapmaya devam etmeli.\" \"to\"dan sonra fiil.","fa":"«برای پرهیز از افولِ آرام، کسب‌وکارِ جاافتاده باید به نوآوری ادامه بدهد». بعد از «to» فعل."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]}],"id":"c-x06-r2-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r2"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"Employees work at their own pace.\" This means they...","options":["work as fast or slowly as suits them","work at home","work in pairs"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Your own pace = your own speed.","tr":"Kendi hızın = kendi temponla.","fa":"با سرعت خودت یعنی با ریتم خودت."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":3,"prompt":"A flow-chart says \"run out of money\". Which words in a text mean the same?","options":["borrow money","make a profit","have no cash left"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"To run out of cash = to have none left.","tr":"Nakdin tükenmesi = hiç kalmaması.","fa":"تمام شدن پول نقد یعنی چیزی باقی نماندن."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"A table has the columns \"Type\", \"What it involves\" and \"Main benefit\". The gap is in \"Main benefit\". What do you look for?","options":["a description of the activity","the advantage the text gives for that type","the name of the training"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Each column asks for a different fact; the benefit is the advantage.","tr":"Her sütun farklı bir bilgi ister; fayda avantajdır.","fa":"هر ستون اطلاعات متفاوتی می‌خواهد؛ فایده یعنی مزیت."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Box: \"apply for a bank ___ (ONE WORD ONLY)\". The text says \"apply for a bank loan\". Which answer breaks the limit?","options":["bank loan","loan","both are fine"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"bank\" is printed; writing it again makes two words.","tr":"\"bank\" yazılı; onu tekrar yazmak iki kelime eder.","fa":"«bank» چاپ شده؛ نوشتن دوباره‌اش دو کلمه می‌شود."}}],"id":"c-x06-r2-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r2"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
